1
00:00:05,670 --> 00:00:08,010
Boy, do I have to urinate.

2
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:11,860
If only there were a solution to that.

3
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:13,070
Seriously.

4
00:00:13,070 --> 00:00:15,960
I feel like I've got a fish tank in my pelvis.

5
00:00:17,210 --> 00:00:18,830
So go to the bathroom.

6
00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:20,150
I can't.

7
00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:22,080
Why not?

8
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:23,480
Because I'm trying to decide

9
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:27,200
between getting an Xbox One or a PS4.

10
00:00:27,830 --> 00:00:30,740
Oh, "Pee." Why'd I say that?

11
00:00:32,550 --> 00:00:35,000
Forgive me for asking a stupid question,

12
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,110
but why are you being stupid?

13
00:00:38,030 --> 00:00:39,490
I'm not being stupid.

14
00:00:39,490 --> 00:00:42,610
I'm employing the work of Dutch researcher, Mirjam Tuk,

15
00:00:42,610 --> 00:00:44,270
who found that people with full bladders

16
00:00:44,270 --> 00:00:46,640
make better decisions.

17
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:50,350
Why did I pee before I decided to move in here?

18
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:53,970
Oh, how'd the audition go?

19
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:54,800
I killed it.

20
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:57,080
I was even able to cry real tears right on the spot.

21
00:00:57,080 --> 00:00:58,390
- Oh, that's great. - I know.

22
00:00:58,390 --> 00:00:59,930
Next time I get pulled over for a speeding ticket,

23
00:00:59,930 --> 00:01:01,860
here come the waterworks.

24
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:04,690
Here come the waterworks!

25
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:10,070
Aren't you gonna ask?

26
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,470
What is this, my first day?

27
00:01:38,070 --> 00:01:40,660
Can I get your opinion on something that happened at work today?

28
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:41,960
- Of course. - Yeah, sure.

29
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:43,370
Okay, well, I did something

30
00:01:43,370 --> 00:01:45,420
that will either make me look like a lovable goof

31
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:50,000
or a horrible monster damned to spend eternity in hell.

32
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:51,610
I'm sure it's lovable.

33
00:01:51,610 --> 00:01:54,250
I'm gonna go with monster. What do you got?

34
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:57,300
Well, there's this lady in our office who's retiring,

35
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:58,740
and they were passing around one of those big cards

36
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:00,700
- for us to sign... - Okay.

37
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:02,140
But no one told me she was in

38
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:04,550
a horrible car accident over the weekend

39
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:06,970
and what I was signing was not a retirement card

40
00:02:06,970 --> 00:02:09,590
but was actually a "get well" card.

41
00:02:09,590 --> 00:02:12,330
I'm liking my odds here.

42
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:15,580
So on the card, in the hospital,

43
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:18,620
next to the woman who's clinging to life are the words,

44
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:21,790
"Hey, Vivian. You deserve this""

45
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:26,580
"And at least with you gone,

46
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:28,540
no one will steal my yogurt out of the fridge."

47
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,510
No!

48
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:36,020
- "LOL. Smiley face." - Oh, my gosh.

49
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:38,870
"P.S. Good luck wherever you wind up."

50
00:02:40,510 --> 00:02:43,430
Why didn't I put money on this?

51
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:46,650
Hey, that's my agent. If I got the part,

52
00:02:46,650 --> 00:02:49,450
it's still the second best thing I've heard all day.

53
00:02:49,450 --> 00:02:50,440
Hello?

54
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,880
Am I a terrible person?

55
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:54,440
No. No, it was a mistake.

56
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:56,190
Am I a terrible person that it crossed my mind

57
00:02:56,190 --> 00:02:58,420
that she might die and never see the card?

58
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:00,790
Now I think you're flirting with the line.

59
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,780
Good news?

60
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:04,370
No, I didn't get it.

61
00:03:04,370 --> 00:03:05,600
I'm so sorry.

62
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,230
- You'll get offered something soon.- I kind of did.

63
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:10,090
The part in that awful horror movie I passed on

64
00:03:10,090 --> 00:03:11,480
came back around.

65
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,510
Apparently, it's mine if I want it.

66
00:03:13,510 --> 00:03:14,620
Are you gonna take it?

67
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:16,000
I don't know what to do.

68
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,720
Maybe you'll get hit by a car and die.

69
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:23,450
LOL, right?

70
00:03:30,410 --> 00:03:32,200
Emily, right?

71
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,410
Yeah...

72
00:03:33,410 --> 00:03:35,770
I-I don't know if you remember me...

73
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,740
From the dating Web site.

74
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:40,150
Your friend e-mailed me because you were afraid to,

75
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:42,190
then you tracked me down and acted like a lunatic?

76
00:03:42,190 --> 00:03:45,000
Yes, Rajesh Koothrappali.

77
00:03:45,550 --> 00:03:47,350
Look, uh, I just...

78
00:03:47,350 --> 00:03:49,310
I wanted to say I'm sorry.

79
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:50,780
Okay? You were, like,

80
00:03:50,780 --> 00:03:52,570
the coolest person I ever found online,

81
00:03:52,570 --> 00:03:54,240
and I got really nervous

82
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:56,880
and I-I just blew it.

83
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:59,160
Uh, don't worry about it.

84
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:01,060
And if it makes you feel any better,

85
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:03,600
you're not the weirdest guy I've met off the Internet.

86
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:07,170
Well, give me a chance-- you don't even know me.

87
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:10,690
All right,

88
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,600
here's your chance.

89
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:14,900
Wha... Really?

90
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:16,810
Thank you.

91
00:04:16,810 --> 00:04:18,420
Fate has given me a rare second chance,

92
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:21,020
and I swear to Vishnu I'm not gonna blow it.

93
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:24,940
Or normal words followed by a charming smile.

94
00:04:29,490 --> 00:04:32,220
So, first there was PlayStation-- aka PS1--

95
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:35,320
then PS2, PS3 and now PS4.

96
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:36,550
And that makes sense.

97
00:04:36,550 --> 00:04:39,320
You'd think after Xbox, there'd be Xbox 2.

98
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:43,110
But no, next came Xbox 360.

99
00:04:43,110 --> 00:04:47,260
And now, after 360, comes Xbox One.

100
00:04:47,970 --> 00:04:49,430
Why "One"?

101
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:52,820
Maybe that's how many seconds of thought they put into naming it.

102
00:04:53,570 --> 00:04:54,920
Can you get the butter, please?

103
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:57,720
You know, however, with the Xbox One,

104
00:04:57,720 --> 00:05:00,170
I can control my entire entertainment system

105
00:05:00,170 --> 00:05:01,700
using voice commands.

106
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:04,510
Up until now, I've had to use Leonard.

107
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:07,560
Then get the other one. Pass the butter.

108
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:09,530
Get... Hang on.

109
00:05:09,530 --> 00:05:12,770
I don't feel like you're taking this dilemma seriously.

110
00:05:13,850 --> 00:05:15,510
Fine, Sheldon.

111
00:05:15,510 --> 00:05:17,230
You have my undivided attention.

112
00:05:17,230 --> 00:05:20,120
Okay, now, the PS4 is

113
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:22,080
more angular and sleek-looking.

114
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:24,670
- No way. - Yeah, well, it's true.

115
00:05:24,670 --> 00:05:27,150
But the larger size of the Xbox One

116
00:05:27,150 --> 00:05:28,650
may keep it from overheating.

117
00:05:28,650 --> 00:05:30,910
Well, you wouldn't want your gaming system to overheat.

118
00:05:30,910 --> 00:05:33,020
No, see? Well, you absolutely would not.

119
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:34,920
And furthermore, the Xbox One

120
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,960
now comes with a Kinect included.

121
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:39,380
- Included?! - Yes!

122
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:41,590
Not sold separately.

123
00:05:41,590 --> 00:05:43,910
Although...the PS4

124
00:05:43,910 --> 00:05:46,080
uses cool new GDDR5 RAM,

125
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:49,350
while the Xbox One is still using the conventional DDR3 memory.

126
00:05:49,350 --> 00:05:51,380
Why would they still be using DDR3?

127
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:53,420
Are they nuts?!

128
00:05:54,630 --> 00:05:56,060
See? That's what I thought.

129
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:58,980
But then they go and throw in an eSRAM buffer.

130
00:05:58,980 --> 00:05:59,710
Whoa, whoa. Wait a second.

131
00:05:59,710 --> 00:06:01,990
- Who's "they"? - Xbox.

132
00:06:01,990 --> 00:06:04,610
- You're kidding! - No, I am not!

133
00:06:04,610 --> 00:06:06,940
And this eSRAM buffer should totally bridge

134
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:08,770
the 100-gigabit-per-second bandwidth gap

135
00:06:08,770 --> 00:06:10,030
between the two RAM types.

136
00:06:10,030 --> 00:06:12,870
This is a nightmare. How will you ever make a decision?

137
00:06:12,870 --> 00:06:14,130
You see? I don't know!

138
00:06:14,130 --> 00:06:15,090
What should I do?

139
00:06:15,090 --> 00:06:17,530
Please pass the butter!

140
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:29,740
Okay, it's not me, right? This script is terrible.

141
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:31,270
Yeah.

142
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:33,910
I had higher hopes for a movie called

143
00:06:33,910 --> 00:06:37,860
Serial Ape-ist 2: Monkey See, Monkey Kill.

144
00:06:40,290 --> 00:06:41,500
You know, it's still possible

145
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,630
for you to be good in a bad movie.

146
00:06:43,630 --> 00:06:44,750
Okay.

147
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:48,660
"Sometimes I feel like I can control

148
00:06:48,660 --> 00:06:50,690
the killer gorilla instinct inside of me,

149
00:06:50,690 --> 00:06:53,500
but then I see these bananas and I...

150
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:56,720
just want to eat them and then kill people."

151
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:01,630
What am I gonna do?

152
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:04,100
Well, for starters, I wouldn't eat the bananas.

153
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:06,420
No...Come on!

154
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:08,360
This is serious.

155
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:09,980
Does it at least pay well?

156
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:12,500
Less than I was making at The Cheesecake Factory.

157
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:13,730
What does your agent think?

158
00:07:13,730 --> 00:07:16,670
She's thinking of taking a job at The Cheesecake Factory.

159
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:20,410
You know what, why don't you just do it?

160
00:07:20,410 --> 00:07:22,750
You'll go have fun for a few weeks, make some money--

161
00:07:22,750 --> 00:07:24,970
and who knows what it might lead to?

162
00:07:24,970 --> 00:07:26,340
Okay, look, here, page 58.

163
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:29,650
I oil-wrestle an orangutan in a bikini.

164
00:07:30,410 --> 00:07:33,730
Just to clarify, which one of you is wearing the bikini?

165
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:36,150
Both of us.

166
00:07:37,570 --> 00:07:40,320
So it's a family film.

167
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,610
Thank you again for dinner.

168
00:07:44,610 --> 00:07:45,640
You're welcome.

169
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:46,670
Good night.

170
00:07:46,670 --> 00:07:49,340
Uh, it's date night.

171
00:07:49,340 --> 00:07:52,830
Aren't you, uh, forgetting something?

172
00:07:53,290 --> 00:07:55,560
Oh, of course.

173
00:08:02,090 --> 00:08:05,860
Did I mention the PS4 controllers light up?

174
00:08:08,190 --> 00:08:09,810
No.

175
00:08:10,210 --> 00:08:12,820
Well, they do.

176
00:08:16,050 --> 00:08:18,240
And then after coffee, we went for a walk

177
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:20,520
and she told me she always thought people from India

178
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:21,890
were exotic and mysterious.

179
00:08:21,890 --> 00:08:23,620
So, with my mouth, I said,

180
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:25,000
"we're just like anybody else,"

181
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,490
but with my eyes, I said,

182
00:08:26,490 --> 00:08:29,400
"Straight up, Red, hop on my flying carpet."

183
00:08:32,110 --> 00:08:33,530
So, you gonna see her again?

184
00:08:33,530 --> 00:08:34,960
Yeah, we have plans this weekend.

185
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:36,120
And if it's a clear night,

186
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:39,910
I'm gonna lay some romantic astronomy on her.

187
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:42,010
Okay, like what? Show me.

188
00:08:42,010 --> 00:08:43,820
I can't do that to Leonard.

189
00:08:43,820 --> 00:08:47,240
This is some powerful panty-dropping stuff.

190
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:51,850
You have my blessing. Go for it.

191
00:08:51,850 --> 00:08:53,330
Okay.

192
00:08:55,110 --> 00:08:56,540
Penny,

193
00:08:57,540 --> 00:09:00,330
two of the brightest stars in the night sky

194
00:09:00,330 --> 00:09:02,460
are Altair and Vega.

195
00:09:02,460 --> 00:09:05,160
And it is said they were deeply in love

196
00:09:05,230 --> 00:09:07,030
but forever separated

197
00:09:07,030 --> 00:09:09,490
by the celestial river of the Milky Way.

198
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:11,390
- Oh, that's sad. - It is.

199
00:09:11,390 --> 00:09:13,970
But once a year,

200
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:16,730
on the seventh day of the seventh month,

201
00:09:16,730 --> 00:09:18,630
Vega cries so hard

202
00:09:18,630 --> 00:09:21,190
that all the magpies in the world fly up

203
00:09:21,190 --> 00:09:23,410
and create a bridge with their wings

204
00:09:23,410 --> 00:09:25,440
so the two lovers can be together

205
00:09:25,450 --> 00:09:27,470
for a single night

206
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:30,000
of passion.

207
00:09:34,790 --> 00:09:36,690
Okay, that's enough.

208
00:09:39,890 --> 00:09:43,100
Quick poll: PS4 or Xbox One?

209
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:43,780
Raj.

210
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:45,160
- Uh, Xbox One. - Penny.

211
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:46,420
Huh?

212
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:48,620
- Leonard. - PS4.

213
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:50,500
- Wolowitz. - Both great.

214
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:53,470
- Bernadette. - I like the Wii.

215
00:09:55,470 --> 00:09:57,380
Thanks, Grandma.

216
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:01,580
- Oh, my Goodness. - What's up?

217
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:04,270
I just got an e-mail from my ex-girlfriend Lucy.

218
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:07,040
She... misses me and wants to get together.

219
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:09,100
Two women at the same time?

220
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:12,010
Nice job, playa!

221
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,870
Really?

222
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:19,280
Was it the "two women" thing or the "playa"?

223
00:10:20,190 --> 00:10:22,390
It was the "Playa".

224
00:10:26,570 --> 00:10:27,780
What am I supposed to do?

225
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:30,650
How am I supposed to choose between Emily and Lucy?

226
00:10:30,650 --> 00:10:32,770
Why do you have to choose? Date both of them.

227
00:10:32,770 --> 00:10:35,200
I can't date two women at once.

228
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:37,800
Zero women-- that's my sweet spot.

229
00:10:39,270 --> 00:10:40,380
Unless you're sleeping with one of them,

230
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:42,370
seeing other people isn't a big deal.

231
00:10:42,370 --> 00:10:43,530
But what if one of them asks me

232
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:45,310
what I was up to the night before

233
00:10:45,310 --> 00:10:46,790
and I was with the other one?

234
00:10:46,790 --> 00:10:48,280
Then, what, do I lie?

235
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:50,170
- Yes. - Yes.

236
00:10:52,570 --> 00:10:53,950
What do you mean, yes?

237
00:10:53,950 --> 00:10:55,430
What do you mean, yes?

238
00:10:55,430 --> 00:10:57,620
Were you seeing other women when we started dating?

239
00:10:57,620 --> 00:10:59,280
No. Were you seeing other men?

240
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:00,750
No.

241
00:11:00,750 --> 00:11:01,890
Were you seeing other men?

242
00:11:01,890 --> 00:11:03,470
No.

243
00:11:08,820 --> 00:11:11,300
Aren't you gonna ask me?

244
00:11:12,770 --> 00:11:14,730
Come on, really?

245
00:11:17,590 --> 00:11:19,770
Thank you so much for letting us pick your brain.

246
00:11:19,770 --> 00:11:21,050
Yeah, happy to help.

247
00:11:21,050 --> 00:11:22,060
So, what's going on?

248
00:11:22,060 --> 00:11:23,560
Well, I'm having an impossible time

249
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:25,150
getting my career off the ground,

250
00:11:25,150 --> 00:11:27,570
and I got offered a role in this crappy horror movie,

251
00:11:27,570 --> 00:11:29,370
and I just don't know if I should take it.

252
00:11:29,370 --> 00:11:32,300
Well, I have certainly taken some jobs that I've been embarrassed by.

253
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:36,130
I wouldn't exactly call Star Trek embarrassing.

254
00:11:37,670 --> 00:11:39,700
I wasn't.

255
00:11:41,540 --> 00:11:43,590
Me, either.

256
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:45,510
So, what do you think,

257
00:11:45,510 --> 00:11:48,260
is there a professional downside to doing it?

258
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:49,480
Well, it's tricky.

259
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:52,600
You want to take projects that you're excited about,

260
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:55,070
but sometimes you also have to pay the bills.

261
00:11:55,070 --> 00:11:57,610
When you're on the set working on something

262
00:11:57,610 --> 00:11:59,820
that you just know in your heart is bad--

263
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:01,380
not Star Trek...

264
00:12:02,650 --> 00:12:05,250
Yeah, beam me up. I love it!

265
00:12:07,450 --> 00:12:10,920
Anyway, those jobs can be soul-crushing.

266
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:12,450
That's what I'm afraid of.

267
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:15,120
Well, I was in Stand By Me when I was a kid,

268
00:12:15,130 --> 00:12:16,590
and it was a huge success.

269
00:12:16,590 --> 00:12:18,990
The terrible movies I did came after that.

270
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,760
I mean, imagine how that feels.

271
00:12:20,770 --> 00:12:22,220
Sounds rough.

272
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:24,530
I'm telling you, this business is brutal.

273
00:12:24,530 --> 00:12:27,780
To this day, I hate going on auditions.

274
00:12:27,780 --> 00:12:29,640
Okay, I walk in, and I can just

275
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:32,170
feel them thinking...

276
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:33,880
"He was such a cute kid.

277
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:36,060
What happened to him?"

278
00:12:38,180 --> 00:12:39,720
And then I don't get the job,

279
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:42,880
and I can never find out why.

280
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:44,950
Honestly, I get so depressed,

281
00:12:44,950 --> 00:12:49,080
there are entire weeks that I can't even get out of bed.

282
00:12:51,530 --> 00:12:53,780
Okay, this was helpful.

283
00:12:57,300 --> 00:13:00,000
Any news on your coworker who's in the hospital?

284
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,810
Poor thing, she was in surgery for 18 hours.

285
00:13:02,810 --> 00:13:05,270
She's alive, but she's still in critical condition.

286
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:06,410
Oh, no.

287
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:08,480
The one bit of good news is they put her

288
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:10,610
in a medically induced coma before she read the card.

289
00:13:10,620 --> 00:13:12,970
So, you know, silver linings.

290
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:19,140
Were you like this when I married you?

291
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:23,660
Don't worry about it, buddy.

292
00:13:23,660 --> 00:13:25,200
Okay, bye.

293
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:27,420
That was Wil-- he's feeling a lot better.

294
00:13:27,420 --> 00:13:28,600
Apparently, he's 12-down

295
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:31,070
in the TV Guide crossword puzzle.

296
00:13:32,620 --> 00:13:34,570
Did he help you make a decision about the movie?

297
00:13:34,870 --> 00:13:36,070
No. Did you figure out

298
00:13:36,070 --> 00:13:37,620
what you're gonna do about the two girls?

299
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:39,380
As a matter of fact, I did.

300
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:42,060
I've spent so many years living in fear,

301
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:44,000
saying no to new experiences,

302
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,180
but from now on,

303
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:45,890
I'm gonna say yes--

304
00:13:45,890 --> 00:13:48,240
yes to love, yes to adventure, yes to life;

305
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:51,050
whatever it may be, the answer's going to be yes.

306
00:13:51,990 --> 00:13:53,620
He's gonna die alone, right?

307
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:54,600
- Yeah. - Yes.

308
00:13:57,630 --> 00:13:59,300
I'm proud of you, Sheldon.

309
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:01,060
You know, I'm proud of me, too.

310
00:14:01,070 --> 00:14:02,430
I've done all my research,

311
00:14:02,430 --> 00:14:04,360
I conducted an informal poll,

312
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:06,260
and I've arrived at the rock-solid certainty

313
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:07,760
I've made the right choice.

314
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:08,980
Well, that's got to be a good feeling.

315
00:14:08,980 --> 00:14:10,480
Oh, it is.

316
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:13,050
- Although... - Oh, crap.

317
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:16,730
I had the same feeling when I made my dad

318
00:14:16,730 --> 00:14:19,620
buy a Betamax instead of a VHS.

319
00:14:19,620 --> 00:14:21,160
You were just a little kid.

320
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:23,120
Yeah, a little kid who picked the wrong format

321
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:25,890
to record The MacNeil/Lehrer Report.

322
00:14:26,760 --> 00:14:28,390
I also was certain

323
00:14:28,390 --> 00:14:31,220
that HD DVD would win out over Blu-ray.

324
00:14:31,220 --> 00:14:32,280
How old were you then?

325
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:34,110
Old enough to know better.

326
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:36,820
You know, and now that I think about it,

327
00:14:36,820 --> 00:14:38,980
I stood in front of a case of iPods

328
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:41,300
and I bought a Zune.

329
00:14:44,070 --> 00:14:45,280
What's a Zune?

330
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:47,260
Yeah, exactly.

331
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,760
It's an MP3 player

332
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:52,430
brought to us by the makers of Xbox.

333
00:14:52,430 --> 00:14:54,130
What... no, what are you doing?

334
00:14:54,130 --> 00:14:55,350
No, no, pick that back up.

335
00:14:55,350 --> 00:14:57,550
You know it's good. You did the research.

336
00:14:57,550 --> 00:14:59,410
But what if I'm wrong?

337
00:14:59,730 --> 00:15:01,000
You know what?

338
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:02,960
How about I buy it for you?

339
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:03,640
How about

340
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:05,850
I buy you both?

341
00:15:05,850 --> 00:15:07,830
You know I only have one slot available

342
00:15:07,830 --> 00:15:09,320
in my entertainment center.

343
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:11,330
Then I'll buy you a new entertainment center.

344
00:15:11,330 --> 00:15:13,020
Well, yeah... okay, sure.

345
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:15,070
But which one?

346
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:17,670
How about this?

347
00:15:17,670 --> 00:15:19,830
I've heard that if you flip a coin,

348
00:15:19,830 --> 00:15:21,740
it will tell you how you actually feel.

349
00:15:21,740 --> 00:15:23,050
Because you'll either be disappointed

350
00:15:23,050 --> 00:15:25,020
or excited by the outcome.

351
00:15:25,020 --> 00:15:26,270
Interesting.

352
00:15:26,270 --> 00:15:28,450
So, heads it's PS4,

353
00:15:28,450 --> 00:15:30,650
tails it's Xbox One.

354
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:33,040
All right, I'll try.

355
00:15:37,290 --> 00:15:38,290
What is it?

356
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:39,600
A quarter.

357
00:15:44,170 --> 00:15:45,000
Could have given it back to me.

358
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,690
That was a choice.

359
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:55,080
You look...

360
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,720
you look really pretty tonight.

361
00:15:56,720 --> 00:15:57,850
Thanks.

362
00:15:57,850 --> 00:15:59,130
I love that jacket.

363
00:15:59,130 --> 00:16:01,250
Thank you. Thanks, thanks.

364
00:16:03,810 --> 00:16:05,400
I'm sorry. I can't do this.

365
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:07,520
My... my ex-girlfriend e-mailed me,

366
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:08,820
and I'm seeing her Saturday...

367
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:11,710
And I'm glad you like it-- it's from J. Crew.

368
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:14,840
I don't understand.

369
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:15,750
My friends told me it was okay

370
00:16:15,750 --> 00:16:17,540
to see more than one person at a time,

371
00:16:17,540 --> 00:16:20,370
but it-it feels like I'm being deceitful.

372
00:16:20,370 --> 00:16:22,430
Are you getting back together with her?

373
00:16:22,870 --> 00:16:23,620
No.

374
00:16:23,620 --> 00:16:25,460
I-I... I have no idea.

375
00:16:25,460 --> 00:16:26,960
What would you do?

376
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:30,720
Uh, usually on first dates, I talk about music and stuff,

377
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:33,790
but I was promised weird, so let's do this.

378
00:16:35,050 --> 00:16:36,950
How serious were you two?

379
00:16:36,950 --> 00:16:38,860
Well, to be honest,

380
00:16:38,860 --> 00:16:40,800
we only went on four dates,

381
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:42,480
hugged twice, kissed once,

382
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:46,040
and there was a handshake loaded with sexual innuendo.

383
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:50,370
Wait, so...

384
00:16:50,370 --> 00:16:52,870
a girl you never slept with sent you an e-mail

385
00:16:52,870 --> 00:16:55,700
and you felt so guilty about it that you had to tell me?

386
00:16:55,700 --> 00:16:56,650
Yeah.

387
00:16:57,210 --> 00:16:59,510
That's kind of adorable.

388
00:16:59,510 --> 00:17:01,310
Are you... are you sure?

389
00:17:01,310 --> 00:17:02,910
Because this is the part of the night

390
00:17:02,910 --> 00:17:05,090
where I've said something stupid and the girl usually leaves.

391
00:17:05,090 --> 00:17:06,830
I'm still here.

392
00:17:06,830 --> 00:17:10,040
Yeah, but now you make me wonder what's wrong with you.

393
00:17:11,860 --> 00:17:13,280
We just met.

394
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:16,110
You don't need to tell me about other people you're seeing.

395
00:17:16,110 --> 00:17:17,600
Really?

396
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:19,630
Because "I'm dating two women"

397
00:17:19,630 --> 00:17:23,650
is basically the only cool thing I can say about myself.

398
00:17:34,250 --> 00:17:37,830
On the one hand, the Xbox One has a better camera...

399
00:17:37,830 --> 00:17:41,550
but the PS4 has a removable hard drive.

400
00:17:41,550 --> 00:17:43,400
Thoughts?

401
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:46,600
I can't feel my legs.

402
00:17:49,190 --> 00:17:51,030
Oh... I'm sorry, guys,

403
00:17:51,030 --> 00:17:52,630
but the store closed five minutes ago.

404
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:54,920
But I haven't decided yet.

405
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:55,910
You'll have to come back tomorrow.

406
00:17:55,910 --> 00:17:57,880
The registers are closed.

407
00:18:02,010 --> 00:18:03,520
Let's get you some food.

408
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:05,510
Y-You'll feel better after you eat.

409
00:18:05,510 --> 00:18:07,740
Okay.

410
00:18:07,750 --> 00:18:09,880
What-what do you want, like, Thai food?

411
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:11,330
A... A burger?

412
00:18:11,330 --> 00:18:13,880
I don't know!

413
00:18:24,460 --> 00:18:27,000
Hey, look, a quarter!

414
00:18:36,050 --> 00:18:37,260
How's that feel?

415
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:38,000
Great.

416
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,900
Not like regret at all.

417
00:18:42,890 --> 00:18:44,200
Penny?

418
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:46,890
We're working together!

419
00:18:47,390 --> 00:18:49,700
Awesome!

